      "output": "# Errand — Static review record\n\n**Static review only; I did not run the page or any check. Every verdict below is read from the reports, not reproduced.**\n\n## Spec follows the evidence\nThe spec traces to the OpenHands evidence and marks inference. Event taxonomy (run/file/shot/fetch/ask/plan/step/end) collapses the evidence's ActionEvent/ObservationEvent families; §2 tags each activity line [observed]/[inferred] (e.g. fetch, end card, step-no-panel = [inferred]; run/file/shot/ask = [observed]). The four tabs reduce the evidence's seven (files, commits, planner, tasklist, terminal, browser, usage) and the spec names dropped ones under §1 Out and §11 — a defensible, marked narrowing. Approval maps the confirmation-mode + security_risk path; the secret-request queue is dropped (noted Out). §7 live-agent and in-page VFS correctly reflect the evidence's [server-dependency, inferred] gaps (no runtime, no server model). §11 Unknowns carry explicit defaults. The spec does mark what it inferred.\n\n## Acceptance checks (per test report)\n- **Passing: 51 of 51.** The report gives a 51-count total but the spec enumerates only 30 numbered acceptance tests (1–30); the extra 21 are unenumerated, so I can confirm 1–30 as \"shown passing in aggregate\" but cannot map each number individually — not actually run and not individually itemised in the report.\n- **Failing: 0** in the delivered run. The first run failed exactly **one**: *shell — \"palette filter 'take' lists replay.takeOver first\"* (detail: takeOver not in filtered).\n\n## Planted failures\n- **Caught: 22 of 22** (report). The spec lists only 11 planted (P1–P11, mapped to checks 1,2,3,4,8,9,11,13,14,16,25,28); the other 11 are unenumerated in the spec — caught per the report but not individually traceable here.\n\n## What the fixes changed\nTwo edits: (1) replay registers `replay.takeOver` (camelCase) alongside `replay.takeover`, same effect, so the palette filter finds it first — fixing the one failing test; (2) `U.tests.scratch()` now restores a library snapshot so a session-adding test no longer leaks. Both match failures the kernel flagged.\n\n## Spec parts no check covers (per enumerated 1–30)\nNo numbered test covers: command palette filtering/ordering as spec'd (the fix touched it, but it is a shell test, not in 1–30), shortcuts dialog, theme tokens/colours/layout px (§5), most of the VFS built-ins (cp/mv/head/tail/grep/sort/find/tree/pipes/operators — only wc, sort, js, unknown, write are tested), the live system message/tool schemas text, import/export dialogs' Copy/Download, and status-bar fields. **Not actually run** / not evidenced for anything beyond the report numbers above.",
